WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Picture a factory that has
squeezed out every cost it can.

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.470
No idle machines.

3
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.090
No wasted materials.

4
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.780
No spare staff.

5
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.520
Each unit it makes costs as
little as it possibly could.

6
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.890
Economists call this
productive efficiency.

7
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.850
It sounds like the end of the story.

8
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.660
A firm this lean, surely,

9
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.200
wastes nothing. So can a
firm make goods at the lowest

10
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.390
possible cost and still waste resources?

11
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.240
In this mission, you'll learn
the two separate questions

12
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.390
economists ask about waste.

13
00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:35.830
Then you'll compare how efficient
different kinds of market really are.

14
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:40.200
Your mission: find out what
economists really mean by efficient.
